---
description: WCAG 2.2 AA accessibility checklist for GOV.UK pages
globs: **/*.html,**/*.njk
alwaysApply: false
---

# Accessibility

- [ ] Single `<h1>`, headings in sequential order, no skipped levels.
- [ ] Every input has a real associated `<label>` — never placeholder text as a substitute.
- [ ] Grouped inputs (radios, checkboxes, date parts) use a `fieldset`/`legend`.
- [ ] Error summary at the top of the page, linking to each field; individual errors use the macro's `errorMessage`.
- [ ] Link text describes the destination; use `visuallyHiddenText` where visual context won't reach a screen reader.
- [ ] Focus styles are never removed or overridden.
- [ ] Custom dynamic content that updates without a reload is wrapped in `aria-live="polite"`.
- [ ] Images have appropriate `alt` text; decorative images use `alt=""`.
- [ ] Buttons for actions, links for navigation (start button is the documented exception).

```nunjucks
{{ govukRadios({
  name: "contact",
  fieldset: { legend: { text: "How would you prefer to be contacted?", isPageHeading: true } },
  items: [...]
}) }}
```
